<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>ESP Web Flasher</title>
<style>
  :root{
    --bg:#0f171e; --panel:#16212b; --ink:#dde6ed; --soft:#a2b2bf; --faint:#75889a;
    --rule:#283742; --teal:#48bacc; --good:#5fbf85; --warn:#d6a43c; --bad:#e4736d;
  }
  *,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box}
  body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);
    font:15px/1.6 system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;padding:28px 22px 60px}
  .wrap{max-width:660px;margin:0 auto}
  h1{font-size:1.5rem;margin:0 0 4px;letter-spacing:-.01em}
  .sub{color:var(--soft);margin:0 0 26px;font-size:.95rem}
  .card{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:8px;
    padding:18px 20px;margin:0 0 18px}
  .card h2{font-size:1.02rem;margin:0 0 10px}
  code{font-family:ui-monospace,"SF Mono",Menlo,monospace;font-size:.86em;
    background:#1b2732;color:#cfe;padding:.12em .38em;border-radius:3px}
  ol{margin:0;padding-left:1.2em} li{margin-bottom:.5em}
  a{color:var(--teal)}
  #gate{border-left:3px solid var(--warn)}
  #gate.ok{border-left-color:var(--good)}
  #gate.bad{border-left-color:var(--bad)}
  .badge{display:inline-block;font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.08em;
    text-transform:uppercase;padding:.18em .5em;border-radius:3px;margin-left:.4em}
  .badge.ok{background:#12341f;color:var(--good)}
  .badge.bad{background:#3a1b1a;color:var(--bad)}
  .muted{color:var(--faint);font-size:.88rem}
  esp-web-install-button{display:block;margin-top:12px}
  .why{margin-top:10px;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--soft)}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <h1>ESP Web Flasher</h1>
  <p class="sub">Flash a board and set its Wi-Fi over USB — from this sidebar.</p>

  <!-- Filled in by check.js. Rendered pessimistic so a blocked script never
       leaves a page that looks like it should work. -->
  <div class="card" id="gate">
    <h2>Browser check <span class="badge bad" id="gate-badge">checking…</span></h2>
    <div id="gate-body" class="muted">
      If this text does not change, JavaScript was blocked and the flasher
      cannot run on this page.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Before you connect</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Unplug the board from anything else reading its serial port. A running
        logger or bridge <strong>holds the port</strong> and the browser will not
        see it.<br>
        <span class="muted">On the machine with the board:
        <code>pkill -f serial-to-mqtt</code></span></li>
      <li>Plug the board into <strong>this computer</strong> — the one running the
        browser, not the Home Assistant host.</li>
      <li>Press <em>Connect</em>, choose the serial port, then
        <em>Configure Wi-Fi</em>.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Flash / configure</h2>
    <esp-web-install-button id="btn" manifest="{{MANIFEST_URL}}">
      <button slot="activate">Connect to a board</button>
      <span slot="unsupported">This browser cannot do Web Serial — see the check above.</span>
      <span slot="not-allowed">This page is not a secure context — see the check above.</span>
    </esp-web-install-button>
    <p class="why">Already-flashed boards do not need reflashing: connect, then
      pick <strong>Configure Wi-Fi</strong> to send credentials over Improv.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Workshop gallery</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:0">
      <a href="{{GALLERY_URL}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{GALLERY_URL}}</a>
    </p>
  </div>

</div>

<!-- Same-origin file, never inline: the CSP names script-src 'self', and an
     inline script would be blocked with nothing shown in the page. -->
<script src="check.js"></script>
<script type="module" src="https://unpkg.com/esp-web-tools@9.4.3/dist/web/install-button.js?module"></script>
</body>
</html>
